multi - tennat : 
 Multi-tenant means one application serves multiple clients (tenants), but each client has separate data. 
 In our e-commerce product, different businesses use the same application, but their data is separated using tenant identification.

Shared architecture : 
Shared architecture means all these tenants use the same server, same backend code, and same database structure. 
The infrastructure is shared to reduce cost and make maintenance easy.

So, multi-tenant is about serving multiple clients in one application, and shared architecture is about sharing system resources
 like server and database


In our company, we use the term industry for different platforms like Holiq, Straunt, and Service Front. All these industries use 
the same backend system, but data is separated using tenant ID. This is multi-tenant with shared architecture.

